THE VALIDATION INSTRUMENT WAS WRONG, IN THE FLATTERING DIRECTION. Its first
version compared the WRITTEN module text against project module names, did not
model aliases, and certified "229/229 correctly refused" -- concealing 29
genuine losses, since `alias Mix.Tasks.Phx.Gen` + `Gen.Context.build` is a real
first-party call. Rewritten to IMPORT the shipped `_extract_alias_hints` /
`_expand_alias`, it found them. A validation instrument that does not model the
thing under test will exonerate it.

One existing test is RE-POINTED, not deleted: `test_dot_call_resolver_fallback`
called `Greeter.greet()` cross-module with NO alias line, which Elixir cannot
resolve and which passed only through the mechanism this commit removes. Its
own docstring always said "short module alias"; the alias is now written.

Filed, not folded: a function reached only through `defdelegate`
(`Phoenix.CodeReloader.sync/0`) registers no symbol under its own module and
now goes unresolved rather than binding to the delegate target's module --
which was the wrong module anyway.

